CORE broken-smt-backend no-new-smt wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constant-offset pointer-array byte_extract: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ symbolic-offset pointer-array byte_extract: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Reads a pointer back out of an array of pointers via a byte_extract, at both
a constant and a symbolic byte offset, exercising the wide pointer encoding's
convert_byte_extract pointer-array handling (constant-offset slice and
symbolic-offset multiplexer).
